        <p>A. H. CROSFIELD, FRED MADDISON. HARRY NEW. Supported by Alderman Tinnion' J.P., Aldermen W. Pierpornt, J.P., Councillors J. Wilkinson,nson, J.P., J. T. Locker, J.P.. Megan. Elba Armitage, J.P., T. Pemberton, J.P., J. U. Withinshaw, P. Pennock end others. CHAIRMAN C. E. PARKER, J.P. The new Liberal Lecture Van will be opened at the commencement of the Meeting by A. H. CROSFIELD. ALL ROADS LZAD To 13111D01 FOOT. WORKINGMEN'S INFIRMARY COMMITTEE THE THIRD ANNUAL OPEN-AIR MUSICAL FESTIVAL WILL BR HNLD IN BANK PARK (By kind permiseion of the Mayor end Corporation), on SUNDAY. JULY germ, AT 3.15 rot. THE COMBINED MALE VOICE CHOIRS (Conductor : Mr. F. Hickman). THE WARRINGTON MALE VOICE CHOIR AND THE APOLLA MALE VOICE CHOIR, WITH CROSFIELD'S BAND (Condeetor : Mr. W. Ifelliwell) WILL HAND= A CHOWN SILLSCTION OF blouse. There will be no charge for exhalation to the Park, bat there will he a Collection at th• Utter., to which all mill be expected tcscontribute. A number of chairs for which a snail charge will b• Nude will be provided. Programmes free. THOMAS BURTON, Chairmen. J. H. J. HAMPSON, Hon. Secretary. COUNTY BOROUGH OF WAR RINGTO N SANKEY SANATORIUM. COOK•GENERAL Wanted for shove Institution to cook for staff and patients and to assist in general housework of Nurses' Homo—Apply MATRON, Atkin at., Hospital. LIVERPOOL AND NORTH WALES DAILY SAILING S (SUNDAYS INCLUDED) 10.45 ate. Every Day, by "1.. Marguerite " for Llandudno (a hour. rebore), Besomaris, Bangor and Monti Bridge, due beck 7.30 p.m. 2.15 p.m. Extra Sail; nip, Friday., Saturdays, Sundays end Mondays for Llandudno end blend i Streit.. For all further informa- tion end oonditions of carriage apply to the Liverpool and North Wales Steamship Comp.), Ltd. T. G. Brom, Secretary. 10. Chapel at., Liverpool. LANG LAN OS' SAILINGS to GREENOCK and GLASGOW. " PRINCESS LOUISE " or other STEAMER From LIVERPOOL From GLASGOW. (Clarence dock). (Berths No. 22-28 North side) , Bat. July 22.7 p.m. Toes. July 25, 3 p.