      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-07-22_WidnesExaminer_art0005" n="art0005">
        <head>PART X. SANITARY PROVISIONS.</head>
        <p>PART X. SANITARY PROVISIONS.</p>
        <p>CORPORATIO?"1-.MAY MAU COMMUNICATIONS BISTWISEN PRIVATE UHAI,I9 AND THIMIt SXW ERS ON r•Y• ENT of,C. . _</p>
        <p>54. If the OWDar or occupier of any premikes within the borough deeirea that the sewer or drain from such premise. shall be made to commuuicate with any sewer of the Corporation such communication shall be made by the Corporation upon the coot or estimated cost of mAing the communication being paid to the Corporetion or the payment thereof to them being secured to their satisfaction and the Corporation may eaecute all works necessary for that purpose. AIIENDIOLST Or SuorrioB 19 or PUBLIC Rostra ACT ASIONDI(NOT Aur 1890.</p>
        <p>55. The powers giseu by section 19 of the Poblic Health Acts Amendmeot Act 1890 In relation to tee or more houses belonging to different owners shall extend sod apply tj two or more houses belonging to tbe same</p>
        <p>I lore PREVENTING SOIL AND SAND PROJI BEING SVASIIED INTO STRLETs. MI. (I) lageowners or occupiers of all lands abutting upon any public street and the owners or occupiers of all lands abutting upon or adjoining any private street communicating with any public street shall so farms off channel or mahout theit lands.. to prevent the soil and sand of such lands front falling upon or being washed or carried into any public street sewer or gully in each quantities as will obetruct the highway or choke up such boots' or gully. (2) Any person who shall offend against this election shall he liable to a penalty not *Heeding five pound. end ton daily penally not exceeding forty shilling. (3) For the purpose of this section" public etrest means a street repairable by the inhabitant. at large. WATERCOURSES NOT TO US COVERED IN EXCEPT IN AR!2ORDANC. WITH APPROVED PLAN.</p>
        <p>_ . 57. Before the owner of any laud within the borough ahall culvert or cover over any watercourses thereon forming part of the natural drainage of the area Involved he shall usbmit fur the approval of the Corporation plans motions and specification. of such watercourse, and the method of cuivertirg or covering In the same and the Corporation may reinject as hereinafter provided require such owner to no construct any such culvert or so to cover any such water courses as to secure the free and uninterrupted pauage of the water flowing in any such watercourue. , If any difference shall arise between the Corporation I and such owner a. to the expediency necessity or other- wlse of the works required by the Corporatios to be executed such difference shall be referred to arbitration and the provisions of the Arbitration Act 1880 shall apply thereto. Any person offending against this section shall be liable to a penalty not exceeding ,C 5 and to • daily penalty not exceeding forty shillings. 1111• ROPER CONTRUCTION Oft ittl'Alß OF WATER- -1.0,1a OR DRAIN.</p>
        <p>58. If a watercloeet drain or soil pipe is so con• structsd or repaired as to be a nuisanc, or injurious or dangerous to health the person who undertook or executed such construction or repair shall unless be shows that such construction or repair was nut due to any wilful act neglect or default be liable to a penalty not exceeding twenty pounds. Provided that where. person is charged sith an offence under this motion he shall be entitled upon information duly laid by him to have any other person being his agent servant or work- man shorn he charges as the actual offender brought before the court at the time oppointed for hearing the charge and if he proves to the aatlsfaction of the court that be had used due diligence to prevent the commis- Ilion of the offence and that the slid other person corn• , ruitted the offence without his knowledge consent or : connivance he shall be exempt, from any penalty and the said other person may he aummarily convicted of tie offence.</p>
        <p>STREET ORDERLY MYR</p>
        <p>_..—... 59—The Corporation may provide and maintain orderly bins for the collection and temporsry deposit of street refuse in upon Of under the streets of the borough of such dimensions and in such positions as they may from time to time ,ketermino.</p>
        <p>RICO ELATION</p>
        <p>110.—The Corporation or iy by notice to venting require the owner or occupier of any dwelling-house to provide galvanised iron or enamelled iron dustbins for the convenient removal of house refuse and such dust- bins shall be of such size and construction as may be approved by the Corporation and any owner or occupier who fails within fourteen dsys after notice given to him to comply with the requirements of the Corpora- tion shall be liable to a penalty not exceeding twenty shillings and to • deity penalty not esoceding lice shillings. Provided teat this section shall not authorise the Corporation to require the provision of • dustbin thereunder in any case in which a dustbin or aahpit inn-at the passing of this Anti. of sui able sine and in proper order and condition.</p>
        <p>PROHILITION OV BLOWING OR INFLATING CARCASS.</p>
        <p>61 —(0 It shall not be tufto to or to inflate the carcase or any part of the carcase of any suit:nal slaughtered within ot brought into the borough. (2) Aoy person who shall offend against the provimions of subsection (I; of thin section or sirdi expose or deposit for sale a ithin the borough a carcase no blown or Mated or any part thereof shall be liable to a penalty not exceediog twenty shinier. COM YE,NSATION to VEI.ONS Canslso EMPLOY 0 esT.</p>
        <p>_ 62.—if any person shall at the request of the Corporation or of the medical officer stop his employ. tent for the purpose of preventing the spread of infectious disease the Corporation tiny make compensa- tion to him for any loss he may sustaiu by reason of such stoppage. INFORMATION TO Es PCRNIAIIRD To MEDICAL OrrlcEll AND PENALTY EDE reitNISHINO FALSE INFoItMATIoN. 63.—(1) The occupier of say building in the borough which is need for human habitation and in which there is or has been any person suffering from an infectious dimwitse shall on the application of the medical officer at any time during the illness of such person or within six weeka from the cocurrence of such Ulnae. furnish such infor.nation within his knowledge as the medical officer may reasonably require for the purpose of enabling meaeures to be taken to prevent the spread of the disease. Any occupier knowingly furnishing false informa- tion Wall be liable on summary oonviction to a penalty not exceeding forty shillings. (3) In thle erection the expression " occupier " shell have the same meaning im in the Infectious Disease (Notification) Act 1849. Dated this 22nd cloy of July ,1911. J. LYON WHITTLE, Tows Clerk.</p>
