        <p>The fortnightly meeting of the Runcorn Board of Guardians was held st Dutton Workhouse on fuesday afternoon Air J Spruce presiding over a good sttend• anew The °Ricers present were Messrs 0 hi Ashton (clerk), W E Hooch lasmistant clerk), T Gook, Wit de Prez, J F Pearson (relieviog °Ricers) and J Persons (master.) N iTION 11. IN•CRAN,F. PILT</p>
        <p>The Fitlhrm Guardians wroteesking the fl,rvd to sup- port the following resolution and ern • similar one : " That ha•ing regard to the intoning divergence of public opinion as to the merits of the National Insurance Hill and the seriour danger to the entire community involved in the harty ndoption of an nasplickting lied far reaching s meerurn, thie Board errantly entreats the Government not to proceed with the Bill until a more ad./nate opportunity has hen allordel the country of ascertaining how the various interestr of the people are iikely to be rtTected." Mr. Roylence moved that the tesoltdiou lie on the table. Mr. Normrn seconded.</p>
        <p>Florvever, Mr. Jones of Moore. moved that tt.e Board support the resolution and Mr. Mcfntyre seconded. By e good a ajority it rvas decided to support the resolution.</p>
