        <p>The above Battalion ettendod (hi Pariih Church, , Warrington net Rowley morning, the Rector of War- ' rington (the Rev. Canon Willis) being chaplain of the listaalion) By kind perrnimion of Colonel J I) Fehr. clough the Battalion fell in at the Drill Dail and marched to church heeded by the Blue Coat School brass band sod the Battalion bugle band, consisting mainly el lade from Stockton Heath and St. Paul's Companies. There War. about 1011 of all nuke preempt. The attendance would have been larger but Chriat Church, Latchford Company were on duty at their own church for the Jubilee services there. The Honorary Colonel(Colonel litekton,V.l)..was on parade which was under the commend of the Colonel (Major Appleton). !tlej.ir Brooke., C L.B, the Acting Adjutant (Captain I lepherd, C.L.8.), and the Quartermaster (Lieutenant Bunch, C.!.. 11., Sergeant Major Bottoroley and the following Company Officers were A.MIO on parade : Captain Ford, C.L.B. (Stockton Heath Company), Captain and Lientrnant Ilenahall, C.L.8., (Sr. Paul's Company), Lieutenant Coate., C.L.H. (St. Elphin'a Co.), Lieutenant Johnson, CLII, (Padgate Conspaoy). The aerroon was preached by the Rev. T. Vicars (assistant chaplain., and taking Joehits as an *sample of obedience to order, and of self-sacrifice for the 'mad of his command, throughout a moat impressive address he taught all present a most useful lento.. of Chriatlan traolinesa and nelfetcrifice. . . .</p>
        <p>- Both bands played exceedingly well, and it was evident ttat they hid taken Arent pains to practice the music beforehimd. Before ilism6sing the Battalion at the Drill Ball, the Commanding Odic, In the mimeo( tbe Battalion, tkanked the bandit for their services. A C imposite Company will ettenit the North-Weetern Coop at SkeAnens *slip in August, end vvill tie under tie command of Captain !When], C.L.itt,</p>
