        <p>Tile MONOPOLY OF LAND WAS DOOMED (Applause). They teen perfectly well thut to all practical intents end purposes they ears en deed no Queen Anne. They would never again control this country, because their power over land value one abeolutely gone. ( tpplause). Lord Derby, • robust English gentlemen, oneed every yard of land from two miles beyond Senforth stretching towerds Crosby, op to the Jungle, Liverpool. Where did be get it (tom ? lie did not buy or steal it, hut the people of Liverpool gene it to him. kVhen it was weals laud his secretor was appro. need I y the people of Bootle, but would not sell or rent tie land to them. lloweter he said " I will let u.e ii. for a term of 7rars, pro, ired 'hot you make • shore-lend of it—tbat is till it up." The silly fools began to fill It op and tbey msde every yard of that shore-land. To-dey bin lordship of D. rby was drawing rent from land that bud been made by tte hone and eiusw of the people of Liverpool and to which he hod no c .ntributed • braes farthing. (" Shame.") " lie enys to your FOES" con- tinued the speaker "J..in the Terri oil .1e mod defend your country. What fools you archf too follow that ! Ile says 'Join the Neivy and fight under the flug.' What twaddle it all in! How ehuoluorly r inful it is to ask men nl,o do not know from one week to another where their next wets wagon ere coolies from to Dr.FEND A LAND 'NAT A HANDFUL OF MEN DAVE</p>
        <p>STOLEN AND FII,CIIBI,</p>
        <p>eee r front the whole of the population (Applnners). fly thu Vioanoe Bill the control of the land of thin country in in Jour bande. ICeeP it there. Ihe 1101116 of Lord. is told to-dny to steed in the way. Nominally it doee. Rosily it is only • shadow of • !loupe. Very noon it will not even hen shadow. You will he told that you are letting your country go to ruin. On the other band yet, are making it easier for your children to do right end more difficult for them to do wrong. You are told that you will be wiper Meg this country. You cannot pauperise 40,0(0,000 people much more than that there /hall be 15,000,000 out of the 40,0t0,000 with only a thin sheet of paper between , them end shoetree atarystion—an is the case to-dsy." Referring to the opposition of the flume of Lords to Octets Rule, Mr. Ga-side said that behind the House of Lords were the money lenders who really controlled that country, end the Ireland of to-day wee governed through an absentee landlordism by a purse that Ins not held by the landlord. " Yon any the Irish are disloyal " he continued. "Han your mother been taken out of bed when it has been raining, and thrown into a ditch 21Iu your wifeovith a beby one day old,been taken and thrown into a barn under &amp;thatched roof? Plane you been chit bed by a 00134.5b1e became you have tried to prevent the thatch on your house being burnt ? If you have not, you have no right to talk. You tell me the Irish see bad. 1 am Lent:satire born and I tell you they have not been half had enough. If the same things bad been done In Warrington, men would have risen in their thounande, paneled the streets and made each a condition of things ehsolutely impossible." The weight of taxation on the Iriehman averaged 28s. per head es compered with 16t. 6d. paid by the Rnelishman. In °cinchedon the apeaher said he was a patriot and loved kin country, but he believed the safety and well-being of the nation began on the hearthstone of the poorest man or woman in i