        <head>ARITHMETIC AND HOMEWORK.</head>
        <p>ARITHMETIC AND HOMEWORK.</p>
        <p>The School Manngernent Committee hada conference with the head teachers of the public elementary school Rion the matter. arising out of the report of the Director or It:filtration with reference to the teaching of nrithmetio in the FeboolB. Afterwards the snhjecr wne considered by the committee, and 112 the end, it</p>
        <p>elm reaolved that the head teachers of the nenior departments he instructed to arrange for the aubject of arithmetic tote taught in all chimes at one and the FBlllO time, in order that the children may be divided , " ' -</p>
        <p>(according to their attainment) into special nets for this subject and be temporarily transferred from their ordinary claaaen for instruction therein ; and further that the head teachers be instructed to encourage the doing of homewoik by the scholars, The Rev. JAMAS DAVII,I thought they should not tie the hands of the head teachers with regard to the organization of their schools. Ile made bold to any that of all tho subjects taught in the schools arithmetic was the one that could Fe taught without grouping the entire school. The committee could not all claim to be ' experts on educational matters, and for them to tie the hands of the teachers to the fetching of arithmetic all through the schools at the I am, time, was going beyond what was wise. Ile proposed that the minute be referred back. The amendment was not seconded and the minutes were accordingly approved. THE commirrEE AND A PROPOSED PICNIC. At a meeting of the School Mensgement Committee that day, the Chairman ol the Education Coramittee having read correspondence and reported on his action wit', regard to a request for essietanoe to issue tickets in the schoola for a proposed picnic, it was resolved that the action of the Chairman be approved. MR. It. If. ALBERT'S NEW APPOINTMENT. Mr. R. If. Albery, the second master at the Secondary School and Technicel Institute, having obtained another imp Antment. the School Management Committee reaolved that applications be invited for a second master ate salary at the rate of from El to CBS, to be axed according to experience, and a form master at anal.., of £l2O per annum. The minutes were approved.</p>
