        <p>Children's Suniser Camp The annual picnic to the Wstrington Children's Summer Camp at Preetatyn will take place on Thurs- day, August 17th, when many subscribers and fa lends will &amp;atlas, be taking the opportunity of making practical ac tuaintance with the excellent work of the institution.</p>
        <p>fmeatation to a Teacher. Yesterday afternoon Miss Mary Hawthorn was the recipient of • silver cake basket and photo frame enbacribed to by the teachers and scholars of Wycliffe sohool, at which place she has been a teacher for 8 years. 'lke cause of her leaving is on account of her forthcoming marriage to Mr. Fredk Coney made the presentation, and Miss Hawthorn suitably responded. Death of an Octogenarian. We regret to announce the death of Mr. John Evans which took place at his residence, 15, Palmyra-square, on Monday. 'Pl.e deemed gentleman, who was in his eightieth year, had been ailing for some tittle and his death was not entirely unexpeced. He Was • Welshman with a great love for the country of his birth, and was one of the founders of the Welsh Chola in Croafield-street. The interment took place at the Cemetery on Thursday afternoon. Mew Warrington Landing-Pier. Messrs. Joseph Crosfield and Sons, Limited, of Warrington have given artier+ to Vice-Admiral Sir A. Alostyr, Field, acting conservator of the Mersey, of their intention to c magnet at Warrington, in accord- ance with plans and sections deposited at the office of the Mersey Coneervancy, a landing-place tube used in connection with their floating pontoon lauding on the Cheshire side of the river Mersey, and for the convey- ance of their workpeople from the Bank Quay side of the Mersey to their storks on the Cheshire side. The Priory School.—Drawing Examination Results.</p>
        <p>The".l7ll-orw-irtg pupils have been successful in the Royal Dras ing Society Ex uninstions held last month. Division VI. Elisabeth Armstrong. (pass) ; Di•ision IV. Muriel Acton, (honoms); Hilda H. Houghton, (pass) ; Division ill. Muriel Acton. honours) ; Dorothy Fletcher, (pun); Hilda 1.1. Iloughton, (pass) ; Division 11. Muriel Acton, (honours) ; Dorothy Percival (honours); Hermione hluvnon, (honours) ; Annie Armstrong, (piss) ; Ruth Mawson (pass) ; Division I, Muriel Aetna, (boom's) ; Annie ArrnArong (honours) ; Lilian Forrest, (pass); Ruth Mawson, (pass).</p>
