      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-07-22_WidnesExaminer_art0071" n="art0071">
        <head>. . MOTOR CARS for hire by the day or week.—J. S. ARLAND, St to K., Bridge at., Warriogton.—Advt.</head>
        <p>. . MOTOR CARS for hire by the day or week.—J. S. ARLAND, St to K., Bridge at., Warriogton.—Advt.</p>
        <p>Street Collection for Children's Home.</p>
        <p>A street and house to housercollection has been arranged to be made in Warrington during the week aiding July 20th in aid of the National Children's Home, Bonner-road, London, N.E. Established in I 0 for the reception and training of destitute children, the Institution has extended its ministry to almost every phase of child need, the orphan, crippled and afflicted being cared for in country and seaside branches. Mr. Wrlliam Healey is the local honorary secretary for the collection, and he will be pleased to give information as to the work, and receive offers of essistance from friends willing to help. We under- wand that 900 children have been received from Lancashire and Cheshire. The local branch is at Frodsham. Musical Successes. -••-- •</p>
        <p>The following is the repart sent to Miss Maud Jennings, A.V.C.M 140, Wilderspool-road, from Dr. Lewis, D.C.L F.E IS., Mos. Dec.. London : —" Thurs- day evening, 13th inst. : Your candidates did splendidly, and; congratulate you." The examina- tion was held in Manchester, Jule 3rd, in connection with the Victoria College of Music. Senior grade piano Florrie Morris, 4, Museum-street, 90 marks, first class with honours. Intermediate Sylvester Hall, 133, Sankey-street, 90 marks, first class with honours. James Whittingliani, 43, Lovely-lane, 90 marks, first class with honours. Junior grade: Hilda Baker, The Psrk, Penketb, 93 marks first class with honours. Amy Shutt, 10, Froghell-lane, 93 marks fitet class wth honours. Ethel Houghton, 1, I'ike-street, Stockton Heath, SO murk. first class honours. Primary grade Evelyn Fraser, 119, -tiaskell-street, Stockton Heath (who is only nine years dirge) 91 marks first clime with honour., she Living gained an honour's certificate last year with 9:) marks. Trans, Croquet, Cricket sad other outdoor games J. EL Oa HLAND, 51 to 55,Bridge 51, Werrington,--Ad.vt.</p>
