        <head>WARRINGTON SECONDARY SCHOOL.</head>
        <p>WARRINGTON SECONDARY SCHOOL.</p>
        <p>ANNUAL PRIZE DISTRIBUTION.</p>
        <p>A Successful Year.</p>
        <p>The ir.cressing interest which, being taken in the work of the Warrington Municipal Secondary School wan reflected in the birge attendance at the annual prize distritiution held in the Borough Gymnasium on Thursday afternoon. A stratifying yearn work was under review and it is evident that the school has already gained a smithy posi•ion arnong.t the educational institutions of the north The Chairman f the Education Committee (Councillor H. Rhberis) presided and the prizes were distributed by the Mayor (Councillor Dr. Joseph). Amongst those present on the platform were : —The Mayoress (Mira Joseph), Mrs Ramie, Mrs Jackson Holmes, Rev. Jame. Davis., Councillor W H J Jenkins, Mr E Plieetm, Mr ES A Robson flwadmatcer) and Mr J Moore Murray (direct ir of education I</p>
        <p>Others who accepted the invitation to attend were: Rev Canon and Mns Rev B and Mrs Percival, Miss Divide, Rev II H Corsbie, Alderman J and Mrs Evan., Mr sod Mr. Very Davis, Connelllor S and Mrs Steel, Mr and Mrs John Taylor, Mr and Mrs William Isaac, Mr and Zia Fred Paraortage. Mr and Mrs Bar Id Jolley, Mr and if ra Woodcock, Mr. and Mr.. W. Mason, Captain and Mr. Roberta. Apologies for inability to attend were received from Sir Gilbert and Lady Oreenall, Rev Canon and Mrs Stevens n, Mr and Mrs A H Crotfield, Rev /I and Mrs Gray, Mr W P Mends, Mr al d Mrs Robert Pierplinr, 'Jr ar.d Mrs It T Fa i rcl laugh</p>
        <p>Tte CHAIRMAN, having exenesed tetra at the I chasece of Canoe Stevenson, itei.l he wan rn. re ORO • liitle gratilled,ee rhi wean of the Education Committee n—a dbe knew that in expreasing tint opinicn I wee</p>
        <p>Photo]</p>
