        <p>CORONATIOV A. 01 NT,.—The accounts submitted by Mr. J. E. Sacker at the final meetin; of the Coronation Committee showed the total subscription, to bfivA been nearly £lOO, leaving a balance in hand of E 7 it Id, which was at the committee's disposal. Variot a aug- geati..ns Wore made with regard to the disposal of the mold., and ultimately It woe agreed, on the suggestioa of the Secretary (Mr. Wright) to give a portion of the money to the Parish Nur“ Association, arid with the remainder to purchase book prima for the most regular attendefs at Ihireshury, Batton, Moore and Preston Brook Council Schools during the year just completed.</p>
