        <p>Liberal majority THE NEW MEMBER.</p>
        <p>Cecil Bissliopp Harmswerth, the new member. was born in 1869, and educated at Trii.ity College, Dublin. He is a director of the Atirdnamated Preen He unsuccessfully contested the Droitaich Division of Worceeterelure in 1900 and N.E. Lanark in 1901. In 1901; he was elected memter for the Droitwicb "on, but was detested in the election of JunuarY, 1910 He is a br, titer r.f Baron Northcliffe, of Sir Harold Harmsworth, and of Mr. li. L Ilatmaw.rth. the Liberal member for Caithneve.</p>
        <p>THE LATE MR JOHN WATSON, F A.S.</p>
        <p>Well-known Warrington Engineer.</p>
        <p>Photo.</p>
        <p>Birtles.</p>
        <p>Many of our readers will regret to hear f the death which recurred on Sunday, at St. Annes-on-Sea, after a long and painful illness, of Mr. John Watmn. Fit A S., who for the past ten years had teen chief engineer at the works of Messrs. Pearson and Knowles. Warrington. In March of last year he was seized with illness and underwent an ovration at Edinburgh, but he only partially recovered. and gradually lining strength, suddenly collapsed on Sunday morning. Mr. Wat.on served hi. apprentice- ship with Messrs. Yates and 'I horn, the well-known firm of Engincere. of Blackburn. After a s ide experience—hie professional duties haring taken him to nasny parts of the world —he came to Warringtrn. Ile was very well known is rogin• ering and esti onornical circles in Lancashire. Ile was a member of the Manclierver Association of Engineers nod was also associated with the Liverpool and Manchester Astronomical Societies, having been president for some year. of the last-named society, Mr Watson was a winter of St. Georges Presbyterian Church, Blackburn, but since coming to Warrington he had att•miled Wycliffe Congregational Church. Of an uncedentati, us, kMslly I li.position, he enjoyed the rf spelt of a large circle, and hie death will he generally regretted. Mr. Watson was a native of Brouglity Ferry, near [louder, where the funeral took place co Wednesday.</p>
        <p>•</p>
